{
  "case_id": "2017-16-1519",
  "document_hash": "4c3b1ed147a5031b470c985be643e1296560b265c9a9aaadfcdc4f84105bea32",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1519",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4c3b1ed147a5031b470c985be643e1296560b265c9a9aaadfcdc4f84105bea32",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4c3b1ed147a5-0000-0000",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 2,
        "start": 2
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 10:07 a.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner (Daniel L. Geyser)",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1519",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4c3b1ed147a5031b470c985be643e1296560b265c9a9aaadfcdc4f84105bea32",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4c3b1ed147a5-0000-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. GEYSER: Thank you, Mr. Chief Justice, and may it please the Court: The Mandatory Victims Restitution Act covers the cost of lost income and necessary child care, transportation, and other expenses, while participating in the investigation or prosecution of the offense or attending proceedings related to that offense."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1519",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4c3b1ed147a5031b470c985be643e1296560b265c9a9aaadfcdc4f84105bea32",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4c3b1ed147a5-0000-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: If we -- if we accept your view, wouldn't there be a perverse incentive? We would be telling creditors don't -- don't investigate immediately."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1519",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4c3b1ed147a5031b470c985be643e1296560b265c9a9aaadfcdc4f84105bea32",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4c3b1ed147a5-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KENNEDY: Is there a difference -- excuse me. Is there a difference under -- under the bankruptcy law? I -- I assume that if the government's correct in this case, it's not dischargeable in bankruptcy. I just assume that."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "United States",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1519",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4c3b1ed147a5031b470c985be643e1296560b265c9a9aaadfcdc4f84105bea32",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4c3b1ed147a5-0001-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "First, we don't think it's really properly before the Court. This was not pressed or passed upon below. The government did not try to preserve the authority to uphold the restitution award on an entirely different statutory provision."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1519",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4c3b1ed147a5031b470c985be643e1296560b265c9a9aaadfcdc4f84105bea32",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4c3b1ed147a5-0001-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 26,
        "start": 26
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: Are the expenses for bankruptcy here related to the work of the attorneys or the attendance of corporate officers at the hearing?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1519",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4c3b1ed147a5031b470c985be643e1296560b265c9a9aaadfcdc4f84105bea32",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4c3b1ed147a5-0001-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 27,
        "start": 27
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: Well, what about that small subset of fees, if there were any like that, the fees that we charge because we sat in a -- a courtroom during a proceeding?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "United States",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1519",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4c3b1ed147a5031b470c985be643e1296560b265c9a9aaadfcdc4f84105bea32",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4c3b1ed147a5-0001-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 28,
        "start": 28
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "If Congress wanted to have recovery for victims just for showing up at a civil hearing, presumably, they would also want to cover the fees for the hearing, the filing fee for the case, or maybe the attorneys' fees or expert fees, all the normal expenses that people incur in civil proceedings."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "United States",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1519",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4c3b1ed147a5031b470c985be643e1296560b265c9a9aaadfcdc4f84105bea32",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4c3b1ed147a5-0001-0005",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 31,
        "start": 31
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "If you look to page 17 of the government's brief, they say there are tens of thousands of proceedings under the MVRA every year, which is exactly a reason that Congress would not want to burden district judges and burden the sentencing process with these fact-intensive disputes."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Respondent",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1519",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4c3b1ed147a5031b470c985be643e1296560b265c9a9aaadfcdc4f84105bea32",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4c3b1ed147a5-0001-0006",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 33,
        "start": 33
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The Mandatory Victims Restitution Act enables the victim of a crime to recover for its participation in the investigation of the defendant's offense. The statute is not limited to participation in the government's investigation of the offense."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1519",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4c3b1ed147a5031b470c985be643e1296560b265c9a9aaadfcdc4f84105bea32",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4c3b1ed147a5-0001-0008",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 37,
        "start": 37
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GORSUCH: Counsel, you say that the bankruptcy was a proceeding related to the offense because fraud was at issue there too."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Huston",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1519",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4c3b1ed147a5031b470c985be643e1296560b265c9a9aaadfcdc4f84105bea32",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4c3b1ed147a5-0002-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 45,
        "start": 45
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Well, I think I would say this, Your Honor: It's clear -- there's no dispute that a company that's a victim of a fraud, as in this case, can be a victim for purposes of the MVRA. That's acknowledged."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1519",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4c3b1ed147a5031b470c985be643e1296560b265c9a9aaadfcdc4f84105bea32",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4c3b1ed147a5-0002-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 46,
        "start": 46
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Well, if -- if that's the case, if you agree that the purpose here is all about individual victims, doesn't that really pose a serious problem for you?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1519",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4c3b1ed147a5031b470c985be643e1296560b265c9a9aaadfcdc4f84105bea32",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4c3b1ed147a5-0002-0002",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 56,
        "start": 56
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "He stole $25 million in less than two years."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1519",
      "confidence": 0.94,
      "document_hash": "4c3b1ed147a5031b470c985be643e1296560b265c9a9aaadfcdc4f84105bea32",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4c3b1ed147a5-0003-0001",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 67,
        "start": 67
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "3664(f)(1)(A) somehow controls the amount of restitution here. This Court rejected the identical proposition in Hughey when it looked at the Victim and Witness Protection Act. It said that (f)(1)(A) is a procedural statute."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1519",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "4c3b1ed147a5031b470c985be643e1296560b265c9a9aaadfcdc4f84105bea32",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4c3b1ed147a5-0003-0006",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 67,
        "start": 67
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Judge Higginson in his concurrence cited different articles and studies showing the -- the incredible burden and the complexity of determining exactly these sorts of restitution amounts."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1519",
      "confidence": 0.96,
      "document_hash": "4c3b1ed147a5031b470c985be643e1296560b265c9a9aaadfcdc4f84105bea32",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4c3b1ed147a5-0003-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 68,
        "start": 68
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: Did your client point that out to the district court judge here?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1519",
      "confidence": 0.97,
      "document_hash": "4c3b1ed147a5031b470c985be643e1296560b265c9a9aaadfcdc4f84105bea32",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4c3b1ed147a5-0003-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 70,
        "start": 70
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: Thank you, counsel. The case is submitted."
    },
    {
